WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.469
-I saw you in Brooklyn,
by the way, performing your --

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:04.971
your concert, and I was --
-"Madame X."

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:06.005
-"Madame X."
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:07.239
-It was unbelievable.
-Thank you.

00:00:07.239 --> 00:00:09.041
-And I -- What I loved about it

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:11.110
was that you chose
these smaller arenas.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.879
You always do stuff
that no one's doing.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:16.148
You zig when people are zagging.
-Right.

00:00:16.148 --> 00:00:18.117
-[ Laughter ]
-And then, people --

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:20.219
You can quote me on that.

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:22.755
And -- But here's what I was
going to ask you. Do you --

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:24.891
-Did I make any money?
-No.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.792
No, I wasn't going to
ask you that.

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:28.327
-I didn't. [ Laughing ]
-I was going to ask you...

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:31.464
When people take your ideas --
you do all these things first.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.299
-Mm-hmm.
-And then people take your ideas

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.800
and they don't give you credit,
and I go,

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.235
"No, Madonna did that already."

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:38.171
-Yeah, and they also
don't do it as good.

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:39.706
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:40.907
I mean --

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:43.276
-That's -- [ Laughs ]
That's exactly right.

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.945
-That sounds really,
um, arrogant...

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.447
-Yeah.
-...but it's kind of true.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.015
-No.
-Yeah.

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:52.185
-"Madame X."
This is on Paramount+ tomorrow.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:54.386 line:0%
What -- What do you hope
people take away from this,

00:00:54.386 --> 00:00:56.055 line:0%
from watching this documentary?

00:00:56.055 --> 00:01:00.527
-Um, that art is important
in our lives.

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:03.029
I don't think people
emphasize that enough.

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:05.064
-Yeah.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:08.701
-I -- I'm really inspired by
James Baldwin the writer.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.135
-Yeah.
-Have you heard of him?

00:01:10.135 --> 00:01:11.370
-Of course.
-Don't lie.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.339
-I have heard of James Baldwin.
-Okay, yeah.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:18.077
He's -- was a great source of
inspiration for me growing up,

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:21.680
and he was a great source
of inspiration for the show.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:25.318
And one of the things I quote
over and over again in the show

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:27.753
is that artists are here
to disturb the peace.

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:29.389
And so --
-Wow.

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:31.925
-And so I hope
that I have disturbed

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:34.327
not only your peace
this afternoon but...

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.128
-You always disturb my peace.

00:01:36.128 --> 00:01:38.431
-...people's peace
while they watch the show,

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.299
but I mean that in the best way.
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:42.568
You get in good trouble.
-Good trouble.

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:44.403
-Yeah, you really do.

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:46.138
No, no, no!
Now, why would you --

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:48.040
Madonna. Madonna!

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.375
[ Sultry R&amp;B music plays ]

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.477
Stop, stop, stop, stop.
Stop it.

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:53.846
Oh, my heavens.
Stop it. Stop it.

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:56.415
I don't know what to do.
Stop it right now.

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:57.884
Absolutely -- This is --

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:00.319
♪♪

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:02.788
-No one's gonna see anything.
My God.

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:04.157
-Sorry.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.424
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:07.993
Oh, my gosh. Oh, my gosh.

00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:09.262
Every -- Look at this.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:13.132
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:14.700
I don't know what --
I don't what to --

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.670
-Because life is not just
about interviewing kiddies.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.105
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.440
Okay?
-Is that right?

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.040
-Don't you want
to talk to an adult?

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.142
-Is that right? Yeah.

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:24.377
-Let's have some
adult conversation.

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.778
-Are you talking to an adult
right now?

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.080
-I'm not sure.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.614
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.614 --> 00:02:32.018
I'm talking to someone who's --
I feel, like, you're --

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:34.020
You're in some kind of conflict
right now.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.722
-Oh, interesting.

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.956
-Yeah, have you been
to a therapist?

00:02:37.956 --> 00:02:40.926
-I went a -- I went
once or twice. I didn't --

00:02:40.926 --> 00:02:42.995
It wasn't my thing.
-No.

00:02:42.995 --> 00:02:44.597
-Do you go to therapy?

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:47.567
-Um, I just -- I write.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.468
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.468 --> 00:02:51.036
I write.
-So -- So, no?

00:02:51.036 --> 00:02:53.172
-It's a form of therapy.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:54.974
No, I write, and I also hope

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:57.143
that I have good friends

00:02:57.143 --> 00:03:00.112
and I talk my [bleep] out
with people and, you know,

00:03:00.112 --> 00:03:02.148
that's a kind of therapy,
don't you think?

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.782
-I can be your friend.
-You think?

00:03:03.782 --> 00:03:05.251
-Yeah. You should call me.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.019
-You should've -- You know,
you came over to my house once.

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:10.790
-I did. I had a great time.
You introduced me to "Ladybug."

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.259
Um, whatever it's called.
"Miraculous."

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.626
I didn't know what that was.

00:03:14.626 --> 00:03:16.829
-Do your kids watch it?
-Now, because of you.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.631
-Okay.
-I do everything because of you.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.666
Oh, my gosh. Is this like --

00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:22.401
See? This is why
I don't go to therapy.

00:03:22.401 --> 00:03:24.803
It gets -- It gets --
It gets nowhere.

00:03:24.803 --> 00:03:26.305
-You get --
Yep, and it's gonna --

00:03:26.305 --> 00:03:28.207
Just talk to me.
-Do you smoke?

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:29.608
-No.
-Me neither.

00:03:29.608 --> 00:03:31.377
-I don't.
I smoke for photo shoots.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.545
-But you never smoked?
-No.

00:03:33.545 --> 00:03:36.382
-Because of your voice?
-Yeah, I just don't like it.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:38.551
-Yeah, me neither. Do you vape?

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.753
-I'd rather...

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:42.722
I like...opiates.

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.691
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:48.561
-Ridiculous.
I want to show a clip.

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:52.999
Here is Madonna in "Madame X."
Take a look at this.

